<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλοιός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any glutinous substance, gum</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.112
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ γλισχρότατος γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mir.</u>
					844a14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				20.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1220.16
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">iii A. D.</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυοῦ</span> Pap.); esp. <i>oil and dirt</i> scraped off the
			wrestler's skin with the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στλεγγίς</span>,
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				449
			</span></i>: generally, <i>oily sediment</i> in baths, <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				8
			</span></i>, Teles<i><span class="en">
				p.41H.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. παιδικός</span> substitute for
			butter in ointments, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hippiatr.</u>
				69
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλοιός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i>slippery,
				knavish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νωθρός, ἀσθενής</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῶς,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυστακτικῶς</span>
			, Id. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>thick</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλλίολον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CPR</u>
					27.9
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. (For <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλοι-ϝός</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλία,
			γλίνη</span>, etc., Lat. <i>glūs,
			glūten.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
